<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haakon VI of Norway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1340">1340</a>–<a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haakon VI was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1343 to 1380 and also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1362 to 1364. He married Margaret, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark">Valdemar IV of Denmark</a>, in 1363, and their son Olaf inherited both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and Norway. After the deaths of Haakon and Olaf, Margaret united the three Nordic crowns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haakon-vi-of-norway.jpg" alt="Haakon VI of Norway" width="287" height="338" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawing by Hakon Thorsen (d. before 1924) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kong_Haakon_VI_Magnusson_PI_XVII_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Black Death of 1349 cut royal and church revenues sharply, and in 1380 the death of <b>Haakon VI</b> left the crown to his son Olaf, already king of Denmark, beginning more than four centuries of union.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>Margaret I, daughter of Valdemar IV of Denmark and widow of <b>Haakon VI of Norway</b>, became ruler of Denmark and Norway and, after defeating King Albert of Mecklenburg in 1389, of Sweden too.</blockquote><a href="/state/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=61,15&amp;year=1366" aria-label="Sweden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4861 129 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Haakon VI of Norway"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5311 399h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5311 399h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=61,15&amp;year=1366">What was here in 1366? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
